From 1a9eb1a14d353a0f4e2b9e3bca96343992a23eb0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Raing5Days <M202574102@hust.edu.cn>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 12:07:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(v1): adopt platform-neutral runtime-graph-metadata
 contract

Replace the split-batch/unified DUAL_INPLACE key policy with a platform-neutral
runtime graph metadata contract, aligning with the earlier full-graph parallel
replay draft (#123):

- Add CUDAGraphRuntimeMetadata (opaque, is_valid() schema validation) and
  BatchDescriptor.runtime_metadata; drop the scattered DUAL_INPLACE fields so
  core no longer carries platform-specific key semantics.
- dispatch() takes runtime_metadata + allow_runtime_key_registration: a
  validated runtime key is registered only after explicit opt-in, otherwise it
  fails closed to eager without mutating the key registry (safe capture
  lifecycle).
- Remove the default InplaceSplitKeyStrategy / CudagraphKeyStrategy from core;
  capture/replay policy is owned by the platform plugin. Core default is now
  neutral and fail-closed. Keep Platform.get_cudagraph_key_strategy() as the
  dispatcher hook.
- Forward-context isolation stays on threading.local (contextvars.ContextVar is
  incompatible with torch.compile(fullgraph=True) per Ascend precedent).
- initialize_cudagraph_keys now syncs uniform_decode_query_len to the instance
  (alignment/capacity validation relies on it).
- Port #123's dependency-free host tests (forward-context isolation + runtime
  key opt-in / fail-closed / no-mutation / alignment / capacity).

Co-authored-by: converges PR #264 per review.
